WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:04.649
The first day of Pizzamas in Nerdfighteria
is the first day of snow in Missoulaaaaa!

00:00:04.649 --> 00:00:06.029
Good morning, John.

00:00:06.029 --> 00:00:08.790
It's not morning; it is evening.

00:00:08.790 --> 00:00:13.200
I mean it's officially evening, as you can
tell here in Missoula because the sun's going

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:14.460
down, which means it's 4:30.

00:00:14.460 --> 00:00:18.090
When we said two weeks of Brotherhood 2.0
style videos, I should've pointed out that

00:00:18.090 --> 00:00:20.950
that would mean that I would be late with
every video.

00:00:20.950 --> 00:00:24.470
Because during Brotherhood 2.0, I made a video
the day the video got uploaded.

00:00:24.470 --> 00:00:26.720
Which meant I uploaded it at night, every
day.

00:00:26.720 --> 00:00:30.160
I've gotten a bunch of Tumblr asks from people
saying, "Where's your video?

00:00:30.160 --> 00:00:32.960
You said you were going to do a video."

00:00:32.960 --> 00:00:34.579
and I'm like, "It's still Monday!"

00:00:34.579 --> 00:00:39.239
I'm going to go to the park and scream for
a while and then you will get your video.

00:00:39.239 --> 00:00:40.239
Sorry.

00:00:40.239 --> 00:00:42.260
I actually have to make the video, that's
part of the process.

00:00:42.260 --> 00:00:45.309
Oh man, it is cold out!

00:00:45.309 --> 00:00:49.219
I just got a haircut; I filmed a bunch of
stuff earlier at the warehouse; I'm going

00:00:49.219 --> 00:00:50.550
to show you that now.

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:56.120
Previously on Pizzamas we, were just, it was
just like weird things that we were selling.

00:00:56.120 --> 00:00:58.351
For example this a blanket with just your
eye.

00:00:58.351 --> 00:01:02.429
There's a few journals left, so these are
the leftovers from last year's Pizzamas, right

00:01:02.429 --> 00:01:03.429
here.

00:01:03.429 --> 00:01:06.649
We order extra, always, in case people have
returns, so we always end up with a few extra

00:01:06.649 --> 00:01:11.759
of things, and then we tend to give them away
on SciShow or Subbable perks or Project for

00:01:11.759 --> 00:01:12.820
Awesome things.

00:01:12.820 --> 00:01:15.890
The year before that, we just did T-shirts,
and now we're doing a mix.

00:01:15.890 --> 00:01:22.189
We're doing new weird Pizza John Pizzamas
designs and also products that we haven't

00:01:22.189 --> 00:01:24.020
used before or done before.

00:01:24.020 --> 00:01:25.020
This looks dangerous.

00:01:25.020 --> 00:01:27.490
It's always exciting when things come off
of trucks.

00:01:27.490 --> 00:01:28.490
We don't know...

00:01:28.490 --> 00:01:29.490
Matthew Gaydos: What's it gonna be?

00:01:29.490 --> 00:01:30.490
Hank: We don't know what it is all the time.

00:01:30.490 --> 00:01:31.490
Awesome.

00:01:31.490 --> 00:01:32.520
Close it, it's cold out there!

00:01:32.520 --> 00:01:34.079
Thank you for the mugs!

00:01:34.079 --> 00:01:35.079
Ok bye!

00:01:35.079 --> 00:01:36.079
Hey!

00:01:36.079 --> 00:01:37.079
TFIOS mugs!

00:01:37.079 --> 00:01:40.640
Matt: The first one I took out of the box
I was like "Nooo!"

00:01:40.640 --> 00:01:41.640
Hank: And then they got them...

00:01:41.640 --> 00:01:42.640
The rest of the are right.

00:01:42.640 --> 00:01:43.640
Matt: They're very cool.

00:01:43.640 --> 00:01:44.640
Julia: This one is gonna be worth million
dollars.

00:01:44.640 --> 00:01:45.640
Matt: Limited edition.

00:01:45.640 --> 00:01:47.979
Hank: You think you hate packing peanuts,
think of how we feel.

00:01:47.979 --> 00:01:49.259
Katelyn: It's the worst thing.

00:01:49.259 --> 00:01:50.259
Hank: Hey!

00:01:50.259 --> 00:01:52.921
Pizza- John, your face is on a glass!

00:01:52.921 --> 00:01:56.299
Whenever I pack things at the DFTBA Warehouse,
I can't help but think of the Phantom of Hielbronn.

00:01:56.299 --> 00:02:02.390
Between 1993 and 2009, a woman's DNA was found
at 40 different crime scenes, ranging from

00:02:02.390 --> 00:02:08.560
simple burglary to grisly, execution-style
murders in three different countries in Europe.

00:02:08.560 --> 00:02:14.280
By 2008, police had stepped up the hunt for
the woman, a rare case of a female serial

00:02:14.280 --> 00:02:15.280
killer.

00:02:15.280 --> 00:02:18.010
They knew a lot about her, the clothes that
she wore, the drugs that she was addicted

00:02:18.010 --> 00:02:19.010
to.

00:02:19.010 --> 00:02:22.840
They also found her DNA in the car of a man
who was accused of murdering three people.

00:02:22.840 --> 00:02:27.840
Police were totally freaked out because this
man, this murderer, denied all knowledge of

00:02:27.840 --> 00:02:31.610
this woman, as if completely terrified of
informing on her.

00:02:31.610 --> 00:02:35.950
She became known as the Woman Without a Face,
a female Keyser Söze.

00:02:35.950 --> 00:02:40.110
In 2009, it was determined that the owner
of the DNA that they had detected at all these

00:02:40.110 --> 00:02:44.150
crime scenes was a woman who worked at a cotton
swab factory.

00:02:44.150 --> 00:02:48.810
Her DNA was not at the crime scenes, it was
on the Q-Tips!

00:02:48.810 --> 00:02:53.510
They were using the Q-Tips to do the tests,
and the DNA was already on there!

00:02:53.510 --> 00:02:56.380
So that's what I think about when I'm packing
your mugs, how in addition to a mug, I'm also

00:02:56.380 --> 00:02:57.930
sending you some skin cells.

00:02:57.930 --> 00:03:03.610
It drives home how incredibly tiny these cell
really are, and how sophisticated and amazing

00:03:03.610 --> 00:03:06.230
our techniques for detecting them have become.

00:03:06.230 --> 00:03:09.290
So sophisticated that we end up thinking that
a nice woman who works at the cotton swab

00:03:09.290 --> 00:03:11.950
factory is a freaking crime boss.

00:03:11.950 --> 00:03:14.600
Also, you've probably noticed that I've been
wearing a different Pizza John shirt in every

00:03:14.600 --> 00:03:16.180
shot since we came back from the warehouse.

00:03:16.180 --> 00:03:19.350
This one doesn't look particularly interesting,
but..

00:03:19.350 --> 00:03:20.350
Whaaaat?

00:03:20.350 --> 00:03:22.500
Glowing Pizza John!

00:03:22.500 --> 00:03:25.640
You can see my face in the light of the Pizza
John!

00:03:25.640 --> 00:03:27.930
Alright John, I gotta actually finish and
upload this video.

00:03:27.930 --> 00:03:30.800
I'm actually pretty late; I'm a little worried
I might not make it, but let's hope that I

00:03:30.800 --> 00:03:31.800
do!

00:03:31.800 --> 00:03:32.890
And I'll see you on Tuesday!

00:03:32.890 --> 00:03:35.480
Oh, end screen, there's more than just shirts!

